  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Robert Gordon University (RGU) is a public university in Aberdeen, Scotland, founded as Robert Gordon's College in 1750. RGU is best known for energy (oil & gas) engineering, healthcare, pharmacy, business, and architecture — Aberdeen is the UK's energy industry capital. Often top-1 in the UK for graduate employability (Times Higher Education).",
      "International students enter via International College at Robert Gordon University (ICRGU) — Navitas's pathway college on the RGU Garthdee campus. Foundation and Pre-Master programs lead into an RGU Bachelor's or Master's degree."
    ],
    "paragraphsRu": [
      "Robert Gordon University (RGU) — государственный университет в Абердине, Шотландия. Основан как Robert Gordon's College в 1750. Известен энергетической инженерией (oil & gas), healthcare, фармацией, бизнесом и архитектурой — Абердин столица energy-индустрии UK. Часто №1 в UK по трудоустройству выпускников (Times Higher Education).",
      "Международные студенты заходят через International College at Robert Gordon University (ICRGU) — pathway-колледж Navitas на кампусе RGU Garthdee. Foundation и Pre-Master программы ведут в бакалавриат / магистратуру RGU."
    ],
    "keyFacts": [
      "Aberdeen — UK's energy industry capital",
      "Founded 1750 as Robert Gordon's College",
      "Over 16,000 students",
      "Often #1 UK for graduate employability (Times Higher Education)",
      "Energy + petroleum engineering — top in Europe"
    ],
